-- =============================================================================
-- Metadata Sync — v0.1.x
-- =============================================================================
--
-- Generated by `mj sync push --dir metadata` against MJ_MetaCapture: a database
-- built from migrations ONLY — MJ core (60 migrations), bizapps-common,
-- bizapps-tasks, then this app's own migrations — with no prior sync. The push
-- reported 0 errors and emitted
-- metadata/sql_logging/push_2026-08-24T02-16-09-292Z.sql; this file is that
-- output with the three corrections below.
--
-- WHY THIS EXISTS. Everything under metadata/ previously reached a database only
-- because someone ran `mj sync push` by hand. Nothing carried it into a host
-- built from migrations, so a clean deploy came up with the schema and none of
-- the seeded reference data or entity configuration.
--
-- WHAT IT CARRIES (75 statements):
--   20  MJ_BizApps_Accounting: Currencies            (seed)
--    9  MJ_BizApps_Accounting: GL Account Roles      (seed)
--    8  MJ_BizApps_Accounting: Journal Entry Types   (seed)
--   22  MJ: Entity Relationships                     (form chrome, plus the three
--        RelatedRecordCollection declarations CodeGen reads to emit the typed
--        Lines / Dimensions / Members accessors)
--   10  MJ: Entity Actions + Params + Invocations
--    4  MJ: Entity Fields                            (categories, display)
--    1  MJ: Entities
--    1  MJ: Applications
--
-- CORRECTION 1 — SCHEMA PLACEHOLDERS (37 app + 38 core). The emitted SQL
-- carried literal schema names. Core procedures must not be bound to this app's
-- schema: `mj migrate --schema __mj_BizAppsAccounting` binds the flyway default
-- schema placeholder to THIS app, while spUpdateEntityField, spCreateEntityAction
-- and friends exist only in the MJ core schema. So core calls now use the
-- mjSchema placeholder and this app's calls use the flyway default one, matching
-- the schemaPlaceholders mapping mj.config.cjs already declares for CodeGen's SQL
-- output. This hand-pass is required because the sync logger infers a single
-- schema and rewrites core to the flyway default — MemberJunction/MJ#3618.
--
-- CORRECTION 2 — ESCAPED TEMPLATE EXPRESSIONS (21). Captured string values
-- contain dollar-brace template expressions (journal-entry-batch message
-- templates over b.JournalEntryBatchNumber, b.PostingDate, b.Company and
-- friends). Skyway substitutes placeholders across this entire file, so those
-- would read as undeclared placeholders and fail the run. Each is split with the
-- construct MJ's own escaper emits — a CAST of an empty string spliced between
-- the dollar and the brace — which is SQL-equivalent and invisible to the
-- placeholder scanner. Also #3618: this escape is skipped whenever
-- formatAsMigration is off, which is the mode this app must use. Note this
-- header itself names those expressions without their braces, for the same
-- reason.
--
-- CORRECTION 3 — DROPPED 2 UserApplication CREATES. The application sync
-- creates a UserApplication row per active user as a convenience; the capture
-- database had two (System, Anonymous), each with a freshly minted ID and an
-- spCreateUserApplication call. Shipping those would cover only the capture
-- host's users, and would collide on the (UserID, ApplicationID) unique
-- constraint on any host where installing the app already created them — a
-- create, not an update, so the migration would fail. App-user membership is a
-- host concern, not app metadata.
-- =============================================================================

